x86_64-windows  cxx1 emits M's copy constructor, ??0M@@QEAA@AEBU0@@Z, and cl does not - measured on the Windows box. **cl elides `M m = M(2);` into the member as clang does**, which is worth knowing beside the entry in docs/CONFORMANCE.md that has the two oracles disagreeing about elision on a *return*: here they agree with each other and cxx1 is the one making the copy C++11 also permits
